    <\associate|figure>
      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|1>||The two limits of
      Definition <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|def:D09>.
      At every fixed volume the full sequence of spacings is used (vertical
      arrows); the volume limit then runs along the retained indices
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|P<around|(|k|)>> (circled), chosen once for all
      fields and tests.>|<pageref|auto-14>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|2>||Dependency map. An
      arrow means that the later result uses the earlier one; the trace law
      and the products branch off the main route. The coordinate reflection
      spaces and slab bounds use only the volume limit and the field
      calculus; they enter the rotation argument before continuous rotations
      are available, so the order is not circular. The renormalization group
      runs only from the cutoff to the unit scale, and no mass gap is
      used.>|<pageref|auto-25>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|3>||Levels and the
      direction of integration. Level <with|mode|<quote|math>|m> has spacing
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|a<rsub|m>=D<rsub|m><rsup|-1>>; blocking runs
      from the fine level <with|mode|<quote|math>|m+1> to the coarse level
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|m>, so <with|mode|<quote|math>|a<rsub|m+1>\<less\>a<rsub|m>>,
      and the running coupling decreases by about
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<kappa\><rsub|G>log \<ell\><rsub|m>>, so
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<beta\><rsub|m+1>\<gtr\>\<beta\><rsub|m>> to
      leading order. The ratios grow: <with|mode|<quote|math>|log
      \<ell\><rsub|m>\<to\>\<infty\>> and <with|mode|<quote|math>|log
      \<ell\><rsub|m>/log D<rsub|m>\<to\>0>. The endpoint coupling
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|\<beta\>|\<bar\>>> is prescribed at level
      zero, the reference unit of length, which is not a measured mass
      scale.>|<pageref|auto-27>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|4>||Exact covers of two
      flagged sites (dots). (a) One support carries both flags; the dashed
      line marks the larger region its eligibility test inspects. (b) Two
      disjoint supports carry one flag each. Both selections occur in the sum
      of Definition <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|def:D06>,
      which does not choose a canonical cover. (c) Overlapping supports are
      not a cover.>|<pageref|auto-40>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|5>||A transported
      curvature <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<sigma\><rsub|\<gamma\>,\<square\>>=<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|Ad>><around|(|U<rsub|\<gamma\>>|)>*F<rsub|\<square\>><around|(|U|)>>,
      drawn in one coordinate plane: the curvature of the plaquette
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<square\>>
      based at <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|z>
      is carried to the origin along the lattice path
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<gamma\>>.>|<pageref|auto-61>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|6>||The predictor of a
      coarse link <with|mode|<quote|math>|e=<around|(|y,a|)>>. (a) Fine
      connectors between two blocks, each expressed in the frames at its two
      endpoints. (b) When the connectors lie close together in
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|G>,
      their weighted average <with|mode|<quote|math>|<wide|Y|\<bar\>>=<big|sum><rsub|z>w<rsup|<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|av>>><rsub|z>*Y<rsub|e,z>>
      is a matrix just off <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|G>;
      the predictor is its nearest point of
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|G>,
      and the coarse link <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|e>>
      fluctuates about it with weight <with|mode|<quote|math>|e<rsup|-<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|ss>|font-shape|<quote|right>|b>>\<beta\><with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|pr>><around|(|V<rsub|e>*Q<rsub|e><rsup|-1>|)>>>.
      (c) When the connectors are spread out, a single connector
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|Y<rsub|e,z>> is chosen with probability
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|w<rsup|<with|mode|<quote|text>|<with|font-family|<quote|rm>|font-shape|<quote|right>|av>>><rsub|z>>
      and <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|e>> fluctuates about it. This branch
      is part of the definition of the kernel on every configuration where
      the minimum test fails.>|<pageref|auto-75>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|7>||The five reflected
      tori <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Lambda\><rsub|i>> of Lemma
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:D-localization>,
      of sides <with|mode|<quote|math>|2*<around|(|w+i|)>>, drawn for
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|i=0> and <with|mode|<quote|math>|i=4>. A point
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|y> of <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Lambda\><rsub|i>>
      is classified by its distance, through the read radius
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|R>, from each reflection face; at the shifted
      configurations <with|mode|<quote|math>|V<rsub|i,x-<wide|y|~>>>, healthy
      near <with|mode|<quote|math>|x>, the local formula takes the same value
      on a class for all <with|mode|<quote|math>|i>. The boundary layers have
      fixed width, so a boundary class has a number of points of degree at
      most three in <with|mode|<quote|math>|i>, while the interior class
      grows, with degree four and leading coefficient
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|2<rsup|4>>. The fourth difference
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|<big|sum><rsub|i><around|(|-1|)><rsup|i><with|math-level|<quote|1>|<left|(><resize|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-halign|c>|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-lsep|0spc>|<cwith|1|-1|1|1|cell-rsep|0spc>|<table|<row|<cell|4>>|<row|<cell|i>>>>>||<plus|1b|2.5sep>||<minus|1t|2.5sep>><right|)>><around|(|\<cdummy\>|)>>
      annihilates degrees below four, so it removes every boundary class from
      the total and keeps the interior one. The tori are auxiliary evaluation
      domains, not physical volumes, and the cancellation takes place in the
      sum over all points, not term by term.>|<pageref|auto-108>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|8>||The shell flux of
      Definition <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|def:D13>.
      The cutoff <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<chi\>>
      equals one near the insertion <with|mode|<quote|math>|A<around|(|x<rsub|0>|)>>
      and vanishes near the spectators <with|mode|<quote|math>|B<rsub|i><around|(|x<rsub|i>|)>>;
      the current is integrated against <with|mode|<quote|math>|\<nabla\>*\<chi\>>
      on the shaded annulus. Conservation makes the flux independent of
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<chi\>>,
      so the annulus may shrink towards <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|x<rsub|0>>
      or grow until it meets a spectator. It says nothing about flux through
      large spheres. The vanishing of the total angular flux at infinity is
      proved separately: on coordinate lines in Lemma
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:G-collinear-flux>,
      and for all configurations in Lemma
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:G3.1>.>|<pageref|auto-141>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|9>||The squeeze. Only
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|G<rsub|\<Theta\>>> is monotone (Lemma
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:I1.2>).
      For lattice-rounded separations <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsub|i,\<pm\>>\<to\>t<rsub|\<pm\>>>,
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsub|->\<less\>1\<less\>t<rsub|+>>, the outer
      values, times <with|mode|<quote|math>|r<rsub|i><rsup|8>*log<rsup|2><around|(|1/r<rsub|i>|)>>,
      tend to <with|mode|<quote|math>|A<rsub|G>t<rsub|\<pm\>><rsup|-8>> along
      the radii of Lemma <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:I-radii>;
      letting <with|mode|<quote|math>|t<rsub|\<pm\>>\<to\>1> gives the limit
      <with|mode|<quote|math>|A<rsub|G>>. Every null sequence has such a
      subsequence.>|<pageref|auto-160>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|10>||The three scales
      of Lemma <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><reference|lem:J-lattice>.
      Markers start at the insertion resolution
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|a<rsub|j>>,
      are grouped when they cease to be <with|mode|<quote|math>|B<rsub|l><rsup|2>>-separated,
      and reach level <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|m>
      as one group, where one degree-<with|mode|<quote|math>|t> field is
      extracted; the signed residual is matched backward to
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|k<rsub|\<ast\>>>.
      Right: losses and gains up to subpower factors, at fixed truncation (no
      series in <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|D>).>|<pageref|auto-165>>

      <tuple|normal|<surround|<hidden-binding|<tuple>|11>||Left: two
      insertions; the test is Taylor expanded in
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|x<rsub|h><rsup|\<perp\>>>
      at <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<Delta\><rsub|h>>
      where <with|mode|<quote|math>|<around|\||x<rsub|h><rsup|\<perp\>>|\|>\<leqslant\>2*s<rsub|\<ast\>>>,
      and each dyadic shell contributes at most
      <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<rho\>>,
      up to <no-break><specific|screen|<resize|<move|<with|color|<quote|#A0A0FF>|->|-0.3em|>|0em||0em|>><with|mode|<quote|math>|\<rho\><rsup|-\<varepsilon\><rprime|'>>>.
      Right: a nested forest; the parent operator acts on the test first, and
      only operators on disjoint slot sets commute. Both are subtractions of
      separated correlations, not lattice limits at coincident
      points.>|<pageref|auto-167>>
    </associate>
